.TH TABDOCK 1 "@VERSION@" "tabdock" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tabdock \- autohiding side panel with the tabs and containers of Firefox-family browsers
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tabdock
.br
.B tabdock \-\-\fICOMMAND\fR
.br
.B tabdock \-\-debug
.SH DESCRIPTION
tabdock shows the tabs and containers of Firefox-family browsers in a panel at the edge of the screen.
It runs on X11 and on Wayland compositors with layer-shell (labwc, sway).
The Tabdock extension in the browser feeds it.
.PP
There are two ways to run it:
.TP
.B tabdock
Starts the panel. The browser does this when it opens with the extension (setting
.BR start_with_browser ),
or you start it from the Tabdock menu entry, an autostart line or a key.
Only one panel runs at a time.
.TP
.B tabdock \-\-COMMAND
Tells the panel that is already running what to do, and exits.
Bind these to keys in the window manager.
.B Nothing is started by a command:
with no panel running it prints "tabdock: not running" and exits with status 1.
.SH COMMANDS
These work only while the panel is running.
They change the running panel; they do not write to the config file, except
.B \-\-wider
and
.BR \-\-narrower .
.TP
.B \-\-pin
Pin the panel open, or unpin it. Config: \fBpinned\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-icons
Show or hide the site icons. Config: \fBicons\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-side
Switch the panel to the other screen edge. Config: \fBside\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-all
Switch between the browser in use (auto) and all browsers. Config: \fBview\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-wider, \-\-narrower
Make the panel wider or narrower by 40 px. The width is saved to \fBwidth\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-toggle
Show or hide the panel at once. It stays open until toggled again.
Use it with \fBhover = false\fR, where the pointer does not open the panel.
.TP
.B \-\-find
Show the find window, or close it again. Arrows and Enter pick a tab, Escape closes it.
.TP
.B \-\-next, \-\-prev
Highlight the next or previous row.
.TP
.B \-\-open
Open the highlighted tab, or fold or unfold the highlighted browser.
.TP
.B \-\-new\-workspace
Make a new workspace in the browser in use.
.TP
.B \-\-ws\-next, \-\-ws\-prev
Switch to the next or previous workspace of the browser in use.
.SH OTHER OPTIONS
These work without a running panel.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show the help and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-debug
No GUI: print each snapshot to stdout, and read
.BI "activate " tabId ,
.BI "move " "tabId index"
and
.BI "order " cookieStoreId ,...
from stdin. It starts its own panel, so none may be running.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The panel reads
.I ~/.config/tabdock/config.toml
when it starts.
Change a setting there, then quit the panel with the x in its header and start it again,
or send SIGHUP to the panel process to reload the file.
A reload sets
.BR pinned ,
.BR side ,
.B icons
and the other settings back to the file, whatever the commands changed.
.PP
Settings that have no command:
.TP
.B monitor
\fB"outer"\fR, \fB"primary"\fR or an output name such as \fB"HDMI-A-2"\fR.
.TP
.B margin_top, margin_bottom
Pixels between the panel and the top or bottom of the screen.
.TP
.B follow
\fB"last"\fR keeps the last browser while another window is active, \fB"hide"\fR hides the panel.
.TP
.B hover
\fBfalse\fR: the pointer does not open the panel.
.TP
.B badges, bookmarks, history, launch_offline, start_with_browser
Switch features on or off.
.PP
Every setting is explained in the example file (see FILES).
.SH EXAMPLES
Bind a command to a key in labwc, inside
.B <keyboard>
in
.IR ~/.config/labwc/rc.xml ,
then run
.BR "labwc \-\-reconfigure" :
.PP
.nf
<keybind key="W\-grave">
  <action name="Execute" command="tabdock \-\-find" />
</keybind>
.fi
.PP
Start pinned, on the right edge:
.PP
.nf
pinned = true
side = "right"
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/tabdock/config.toml
Settings.
.TP
.I configs/config.toml
The example with every option explained, under the install directory:
.I /usr/share/tabdock
(package) or
.I ~/.local/share/tabdock
(install.sh).
.TP
.I tabdock.xpi
The signed extension, in the package's install directory and on the GitHub release.
Install it in each browser: about:addons, gear icon, Install Add-on From File.
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/tabdock.log
The output of a panel the browser started.
.SH SEE ALSO
Full usage and settings:
.UR https://github.com/musqz/tabdock
.UE .
